PART E -- all-singleton contexts collapse to a hit-count kernel
  If the context is r independent singleton carriers, residual weights are
  symmetric over sectors.  The candidate only sees its hit-count law.
  g_r(t)=Pr(r singleton throws cover a fixed t-sector requirement).
  kernel rows list g_r(t) for t=0..6.
    r=2: (1, 13/49, 2/49, 0, 0, 0, 0)
